Error [jet.InvalidRoute]: Invalid HTTP route `/files/{name}`: use `:name` or final `*name`; braces are not route markers
  --> http_route_path_type.jet:16:16
    |
 16 |     router.get(Path{"/files/{{name}}"}, named)
    |                ^^^^
 Why: Route patterns use one canonical grammar; ambiguous escapes, traversal, duplicate names, and retired markers would make routing and audit metadata disagree
 Fix: Use `:name` for one segment or final `*name` for a catch-all; percent-encode a literal leading `:` or `*`, and never encode `/`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2805

Error [jet.InvalidRoute]: HTTPRouter route path must be a static String or Path
  --> http_route_path_type.jet:19:16
    |
 19 |     router.get(Path{"/area/{area}/:key"}, keyed)
    |                ^^^^
 Why: Router endpoint contracts are fully checked while building; App routes may be computed at runtime
 Fix: Use a literal, a compile-time String constant or a Path without holes, or register the dynamic route on a `web.app()`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2805

Error [jet.BindingTypeMismatch]: This needs String, but the value is Int
  --> http_route_path_type.jet:22:13
    |
 22 |     mux.get(42, keyed)
    |             ^^
 Why: The value here does not have the type required by this declaration
 Fix: Use a value of the required type or convert it explicitly
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0108
